# Security Rules

## File Upload Security
- MIME type validation is mandatory on every upload endpoint (`fileFilter` in Multer)
- Allowed types: `image/jpeg`, `image/png`, `image/webp` only
- Max file size enforced at Multer level (10MB) — never rely on client-side validation alone
- ALWAYS use `path.basename(filename)` before any `fs` operation on user-supplied filenames
  - Prevents path traversal: `../../.env` → `.env` (safe, won't exist in upload dir)
- File content (magic byte) validation is a known gap — adding `file-type` library is the fix

## Input Validation
- Validate all user-supplied strings at the controller boundary before they touch the DB
- Enum fields (type, material, damage, complexity) must be validated against allowed values
- Never trust `req.params`, `req.query`, or `req.body` without validation
- Multer fields: only accept the field name `image` — reject unknown multipart fields

## SQL Injection Prevention
- All SQL uses prepared statements with named parameters (`@param`) — never string interpolation
- This is enforced by architecture: all SQL lives in `db/database.js` prepared at startup

## Secrets and Credentials
- All credentials in `.env` (gitignored) — never in source code, never in logs
- `.env.sample` contains only placeholder values, never real keys
- MinIO credentials (`MINIO_ACCESS_KEY`, `MINIO_SECRET_KEY`) treated as secrets
- OpenAI API key (`OPENAI_API_KEY`) treated as secret — never log it, never return it in API responses

## Rate Limiting
- express-rate-limit is applied globally: 60 requests/minute per IP
- Upload endpoint is the most sensitive — rate limit protects against AI API cost abuse
- Do not remove or raise limits without documenting the reason

## CORS
- `ALLOWED_ORIGIN` env var controls allowed origin — never use `origin: '*'` in production
- Only GET and PATCH for existing resources, POST for creation — no DELETE exposed to frontend

## HTTP Headers
- Do not expose Express version (`app.disable('x-powered-by')` — add if not present)
- Presigned MinIO URLs are time-limited (1 hour TTL) — images are not permanently public

## Known Gaps (documented, not ignored)
1. No magic-byte validation — MIME header spoofing possible. Fix: add `file-type` library.
2. No auth — intentional for MVP (internal network tool). Document in README.
3. No HTTPS enforcement — intended for local/internal use only. Add reverse proxy (nginx + cert) before any external exposure.
4. No EXIF GPS stripping — images may contain location metadata. Fix: add `sharp` strip metadata call before upload.
